-- svigerske 2026-02-16
I can reproduce. These 1e-6 in many constraints are likely problematic.
-- rajgoel 2026-02-16
Was also one of my thoughts. I tried replacing them with 1e-5, but that didnt help.

P.S. My main need is to convert the outcome of expressions like a <= b to boolean. I do this by checking whether b - a <= epsilon or b - a >= 1.1 * epsilon. Let me know if there is a better approch :-)
-- svigerske 2026-02-17
If you add something like `a + s = b` with slack variable `s`, and indicator constraints `z = 1 -> s >= 0`, `z = 0 -> s <= 0` with a binary variable `z`, then `z=1` means `b - a >= 0`, so `a <= b`, and `z=0` means `b - a <= 0`, so `b <= a`. Changing some 0 to 1e-5 may give a better distinction around `a=b`.
